# Keyboard X

## Overview

Keyboard X is a native Android keyboard project implemented in Kotlin. The app includes a real IME service (`InputMethodService`) and a minimal input view used to connect the keyboard UI to the active Android editor.

This repository currently contains:
- the Android native app foundation from Phase 1,
- the CI workflow introduced in Phase 2,
- the Phase 3 IME stabilization work described below.

It does not include the Phase 4 keyboard layout engine or advanced language features.

## Current status

The project is not a full keyboard layout system yet. The repository currently supports the Android IME foundation and input lifecycle needed to build a stable keyboard service without adding external backends or libraries.

### Phase 3 implementation in this repository

- Fixed the real `InputConnection` handling in `KeyboardIMEService` so it uses `currentInputConnection()` from `InputMethodService` without shadowing the Android API.
- Ensured the IME keeps a valid input connection during `onStartInput` and `onStartInputView`.
- Completed `KeyboardInputView` as a real, buildable view for the IME and wired its callback listener to service logic.
- Kept the implementation on Android Native APIs only.
- Left Phase 4 keyboard layout, theming, keys, and advanced language behavior intentionally out of scope.

### Explicit scope boundaries

- Phase 4 keyboard rendering is not implemented here.
- Advanced Arabic/English input logic is not included here.
- No Firebase, Supabase, or external backend services were added.
- No GitHub Actions workflow changes were made in this task.

### Important note

This documentation reflects the code currently present in the repository. The project has not been end-to-end validated in a local Android SDK/emulator session from this environment, so no claim is made here about a verified successful build beyond the repository state itself.

